{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KWUXKayjPNfgr6P7AeG4MK","type":"tool_result","content":"===== CLAUDE.md =====\n# Chat qualification fixture\n\nUse the installed task-spec skill at .agents/skills/task-spec/SKILL.md.\nThe version-matched TaskSpec CLI is `bash \"/private/tmp/taskspec-qualified-engines/3.10.0/bin/taskspec\"`.\nThis is a fresh conversation: derive current state from artifacts.\nFollow the user request within this repository. Do not spawn agents, commit, publish, or change the installed engine.\n===== tasks/.plans/rate-limit/intent.md =====\n---\nschema_version: 1\nkind: delivery-intent\nid: DI-RATE-LIMIT\ntitle: Enforce organization-level request limits with visible decisions\nclaim: proposed\nsource:\n  uri: tests/fixtures/toolkit/blueprint.md\n  captured_at: '2026-08-02T00:00:00Z'\n  sha256: f40ed16c2898b8363dfce1c19e7c3fd539d52810d52b21faeaf59323117af445\nsuccess:\n- A versioned policy schema rejects invalid limits and windows.\n- Resolution produces exactly one effective policy for an organization.\n- Request 101 is denied after 100 allowed requests in the same window.\n- The denial returns a stable reason and emits matching decision telemetry.\nout_of_scope:\n- Replacing provider-owned usage metering.\n- Choosing production storage or deployment infrastructure.\n---\n# Enforce organization-level request limits with visible decisions\n\n## Delivery outcome\n\nFor every organization request, resolve one effective rate-limit policy, deny request 101 when the effective limit is 100, and expose a stable reason plus decision telemetry without changing provider-owned metering.\n\n## Evidence boundary\n\nThis artifact records a **proposed** claim. Its source, capture time,\nand content hash are recorded in frontmatter; the claim is not implementation\nevidence by itself.\n===== tasks/.plans/rate-limit/steel-thread.md =====\n# Steel Thread\n\n1. [`LEG-POLICY-SCHEMA-VALID`](legs/LEG-POLICY-SCHEMA-VALID.md)\n2. [`LEG-EFFECTIVE-POLICY-RESOLVED`](legs/LEG-EFFECTIVE-POLICY-RESOLVED.md)\n3. [`LEG-REQUEST-101-DENIED`](legs/LEG-REQUEST-101-DENIED.md)\n4. [`LEG-DENIAL-REASON-VISIBLE`](legs/LEG-DENIAL-REASON-VISIBLE.md)\n\nThis is a derived critical capability path. It records ordering, not\nimplementation completion or dispatch authority.\n===== tasks/.plans/rate-limit/decisions/ADR-RATE-LIMIT-ORDER.md =====\n---\nschema_version: 1\nkind: decision\nid: ADR-RATE-LIMIT-ORDER\nstatus: accepted\nowner: example-fixture\nrationale: 'The fixture follows the blueprint order: schema, effective policy, request 101 enforcement,\n  then visible reason and decision telemetry.'\n---\n# ADR-RATE-LIMIT-ORDER\n\nStatus: **accepted**\n\nOwner: example-fixture\n\n## Rationale\n\nThe fixture follows the blueprint order: schema, effective policy, request 101 enforcement, then visible reason and decision telemetry.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3e3cdbbf-4173-4b8f-87a0-59f2add0d6fa","uuid":"95d893e6-d1e3-4f2c-a5da-6232bbcb8b1d","timestamp":"2026-09-15T11:03:49.702Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"===== CLAUDE.md =====\n# Chat qualification fixture\n\nUse the installed task-spec skill at .agents/skills/task-spec/SKILL.md.\nThe version-matched TaskSpec CLI is `bash \"/private/tmp/taskspec-qualified-engines/3.10.0/bin/taskspec\"`.\nThis is a fresh conversation: derive current state from artifacts.\nFollow the user request within this repository. Do not spawn agents, commit, publish, or change the installed engine.\n===== tasks/.plans/rate-limit/intent.md =====\n---\nschema_version: 1\nkind: delivery-intent\nid: DI-RATE-LIMIT\ntitle: Enforce organization-level request limits with visible decisions\nclaim: proposed\nsource:\n  uri: tests/fixtures/toolkit/blueprint.md\n  captured_at: '2026-08-02T00:00:00Z'\n  sha256: f40ed16c2898b8363dfce1c19e7c3fd539d52810d52b21faeaf59323117af445\nsuccess:\n- A versioned policy schema rejects invalid limits and windows.\n- Resolution produces exactly 