{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cf57cupYSAoLPcZerNfA8","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## State on disk\n\n`taskspec decompose status rate-limit`:\n\n```\nDECOMPOSE=NEEDS_REVIEW initiative=rate-limit\nplan_not_ready: Delivery plan is not marked ready.\nreview_missing: An accepted delivery-plan review is required.\n```\n\n**Already recorded — I won't re-ask these:**\n- Intent `DI-RATE-LIMIT` (proposed) with 4 success criteria, sourced/hashed to `tests/fixtures/toolkit/blueprint.md`\n- `ADR-RATE-LIMIT-ORDER` — **accepted**: schema → effective policy → request 101 → visible reason/telemetry\n- Metering boundary: objection `OBJ-METERING-SEPARATION` is **FIXED**; provider metering stays out of the steel thread\n- `SEAM_MAP=READY` (4 seams, 4 single-owner lanes), `TASK_GRAPH=READY` (4 S-effort leaves, linear critical path), `contentions: []`, `reviews/` is empty\n\n## The one decision still missing\n\n**Do you accept the proposed topology as the plan of record — and under whose name?** Nothing else is blocking; the plan sits at `DELIVERY_PLAN=NEEDS_REVIEW` purely because no human has signed off on it.\n\nWhat you'd be accepting:\n\n| Lane (owner) | Leg → proof |\n|---|---|\n| LANE-POLICY-CONTRACT (platform-contracts) | Schema accepts valid limits/windows, rejects invalid |\n| LANE-POLICY-RESOLUTION (policy-runtime) | Exactly one effective policy + provenance |\n| LANE-REQUEST-ENFORCEMENT (request-runtime) | Requests 1–100 allowed, 101 denied, same window |\n| LANE-DECISION-VISIBILITY (reliability-interface) | Denial response and telemetry share one stable reason + decision ID |\n\nTo proceed I need two things from you: a **reviewer identity** and a **reason** for the record. Then:\n\n```bash\ntaskspec decompose review rate-limit --accept --reviewer <name> --reason <reason>\n```\n\nTwo notes before you answer:\n\n- `taskspec setup` reports `MISS signing — no repository key`. Review binds the topology through the repository HMAC key, so `taskspec setup signing` has to run first. That's mechanical, not a product decision — say the word and I'll run it, but it creates a repo-private key so I didn't do it unprompted.\n- Review is not a seal. It only marks the plan ready; `compile` → `batch` produce unsealed leaves, and `gate --stamp` is what authorizes execution of a specific revision. Accepting here doesn't dispatch any work."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1030,"cache_read_input_tokens":25455,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1030},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3e3cdbbf-4173-4b8f-87a0-59f2add0d6fa","uuid":"90512eee-5070-4811-a0b2-1d945c67f613","timestamp":"2026-09-15T11:04:47.285Z","request_id":"req_011Cf57cuL2WqxUZYTzohxRY"}
